    runtime:panel('runtime','Choose where it runs.','CPU/RAM, GPU/VRAM, or a hybrid of both. GPU mode still uses some system RAM.',`<div id="memory-meters" class="stats-grid"></div><form id="runtime-form" class="feature-form"><label>Execution mode<select data-setting="executionMode" id="execution-mode"><option value="auto">Automatic · recommended</option><option value="cpu">CPU · RAM</option><option value="gpu">GPU · VRAM (all model layers)</option><option value="hybrid">Hybrid · RAM + VRAM</option></select></label><p id="execution-help" class="feature-note"></p>${number('GPU layers in hybrid mode','gpuLayers',0,999)}${toggle('Keep the context/KV cache in VRAM','kvOnGpu','Turning this off saves VRAM by using system RAM.')}${number('CPU threads','threads',1,256)}<label>Resource profile<select data-setting="performanceMode"><option value="responsive">Keep the desktop responsive</option><option value="balanced">Balanced (use configured threads)</option></select></label>${number('RAM reserved for the system (GiB)','reserveRamGiB',1,16,.5)}<div class="settings-grid">${number('Prompt batch size','batchSize',16,2048)}${number('Micro batch size','microBatchSize',16,512)}</div><div class="action-row"><button class="primary-button">Save runtime settings</button><button id="reload-model" type="button" class="secondary-button">Save & reload model</button><button id="cancel-load" type="button" class="secondary-button">Cancel loading / unload</button></div></form><p class="feature-note">Responsive mode disables busy polling, uses smaller batches, lowers process priority, and skips startup warmup. RAM/VRAM checks are estimates; model architecture and the context cache affect actual usage. Apple Silicon shares unified memory rather than separate RAM and VRAM.</p><div id="runtime-phase" class="feature-note"></div><pre id="runtime-feature-log" class="feature-log"></pre>`)
